\title{Words by length}
\date{2026-03-04T02:24:55Z}
\tag{discrete}

\import{discrete-macros}

\taxon{Example}
\p{Consider the relation #{L} on the set of all English words, where two words are related if and only if they have the same number of letters. This is an [equivalence relation](008Z):}
\ul{\li{\p{Reflexive? Check, each word has the same number of letters as itself.}
}
\li{\p{Symmetric? Check, if #{a} has the same number of letters as #{b}, then #{b} has the same number of letters as #{a}.}
}
\li{\p{Transitive? Check, if #{a} has the same number of letters as #{b}, and #{b} has the same number of letters as #{c}, then #{a} has the same number of letters as #{c}.}
}
}


